# Commits that changed formatting, names or filenames across the whole tree and nothing else.
# `git blame` skips them, so a line's blame still points at the commit that wrote the code
# rather than at the pass that reformatted or renamed it.
#
# Enable once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# One full-length SHA per line. Add a commit here only if it is provably mechanical. For the
# three passes below the evidence was: the token stream of every source file (comments stripped,
# whitespace normalised, string literals preserved exactly) has the same length before and after,
# with every difference an identifier or a string literal; and the Release binaries' .text
# sections are byte-identical across the reformat alone. The reformat is the only one of the
# three where .text can be compared directly -- renaming changes message strings, which moves
# .rodata and shifts every address -- so for the rename passes the token-stream identity is the
# evidence.

